Hi, I'm the Playwright bot and I took a first look.

**Reproduced on tip-of-tree (npm `1.62.0-next`, sha `2bcd8f2`), chromium only.** When a cross-frame promise gets garbage-collected before it settles, CDP returns `{"code":-32000,"message":"Promise was collected"}`, and Playwright rewrites that into the misleading `page.evaluate: Execution context was destroyed, most likely because of a navigation.` — no navigation actually happened. So the "fix cross-frame GC" part is really V8/CDP behavior, but the **wrong error message is on us**: `crExecutionContext.rewriteError` funnels any unrecognized CDP error into the "execution context was destroyed" string. That's the concrete, actionable bug here.

Your workaround (`async () => { await iframeWindow.foo() }`) is sound: awaiting in the parent frame keeps a reference so the promise isn't collected.

<details>
<summary>Minimal repro (condensed from your comment)</summary>

```ts
import { test, expect } from './pageTest';

test('promise collected cross frame', async ({ page, browserName }) => {
  test.skip(browserName !== 'chromium');
  const client = await page.context().newCDPSession(page);
  await page.setContent(`
    <iframe id="child" srcdoc="<script>window.makePromise = () => new Promise(() => {});</script>"></iframe>
    <script>
      window.api = () => document.querySelector('#child').contentWindow.makePromise();
    </script>
  `);
  await page.waitForFunction(() => !!document.querySelector('iframe')?.contentWindow?.['makePromise']);

  const resultPromise = page.evaluate(() => window['api']()).catch(e => e);
  for (let i = 0; i < 20; ++i)
    await client.send('HeapProfiler.collectGarbage');
  const result = await Promise.race([
    resultPromise,
    new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(() => resolve('did not settle'), 5000)),
  ]);
  console.log('RESULT:', result instanceof Error ? result.message : result);
  expect(result).toBeInstanceOf(Error);
});
```

Output: `RESULT: page.evaluate: Execution context was destroyed, most likely because of a navigation.`
</details>

<details>
<summary>What I ran</summary>

- version: tip-of-tree (npm `1.62.0-next`, sha `2bcd8f2`)
- browser: chromium — reproduces. This is Chromium/V8-CDP-specific (`HeapProfiler.collectGarbage` + `Runtime.callFunctionOn` returning `-32000 Promise was collected`); firefox/webkit don't have the equivalent path, so I scoped the repro to chromium.
- The raw CDP error is `Promise was collected`; it's lost because `packages/playwright-core/src/server/chromium/crExecutionContext.ts` `rewriteError()` throws the generic "Execution context was destroyed" for anything not recognized as a JS error or a closed session.
- variation: a plain unretained `new Promise(() => {})` (no iframe) collected by GC reproduces the same message, matching your note.
</details>

Two things a maintainer will want to weigh: whether to surface the real CDP reason (e.g. keep the `Promise was collected` text) instead of the navigation message, and whether Playwright should retain the awaited promise so GC can't collect it mid-flight. I can't tell which they'll pick, but the misleading message is clearly the reproducible bug.


