I have reproduced this without any iframes. Chromium collects the evaluation promise unless it is retained by something in the page. Firefox/WebKit keep it alive.

```ts
test('promise collected', async ({ page }) => {
  const resultPromise = page.evaluate(() => {
    window['createPromise'] = () => new Promise(() => {});
    return window['createPromise']();
  }).catch(e => e);
  for (let i = 0; i < 20; i++)
    await page.requestGC();
  console.log((await resultPromise).message);
});
```

